{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942358-trying-to-figure-out-what-this-means-to-me-cofd-vs-cwod","id":942358,"title":"Trying to figure out what this means to me CofD vs CWoD...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-02T18:11:27-07:00","id":942358,"title":"Trying to figure out what this means to me CofD vs CWoD...","content":"I have been away for awhile. I like the Meta in Classic World of Darkness. I like the resources in NWoD for the mundane or near mundane world. I have almost all of the stuff dealing with regular life, the core books, a lot of vampire, and most of the core books for NWoD because I like the systemic changes. I still want the old Meta. So, if I am reading this correctly then the CoD is now less compatible with and will provide additional difficulties in combining it with CWoD?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T18:16:13-07:00","id":942362,"title":"","content":"The meta is just setting, you should have no problem putting it in your game in any system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T18:36:02-07:00","id":942376,"title":"","content":"So, are you saying you want the setting of the cWoD with the 2e ChroD rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T23:45:25-07:00","id":942536,"title":"","content":"You know, I'm pretty sure the Translation Guides are gonna get a 2e update soon enough, if nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T14:41:21-07:00","id":948865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942358-trying-to-figure-out-what-this-means-to-me-cofd-vs-cwod?p=942376#post942376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, are you saying you want the setting of the cWoD with the 2e ChroD rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I am not sure. This would require that I read the CoD. I don't know that I want to read them. One of the reasons I quit playing AD&amp;D at age 14 is because I got tired of rules changes, that was when they created 2.0 and suddenly nothing was compatible with what I already owned. It takes days, weeks, even months to put together something depending on how in depth one wishes to go. To then have to translate everything afterwords is simply undesirable and doubles or triples the work load for playing. I have been slowly collecting materials for NWoD and some CWoD, and 20ed. One of my favorite books sitting in front of me right now is Axis Mundi.<br /> <br /> I like some of the streamlining in NWoD. I like the change of abilities from Charisma to Presence and from Appearance to Composure. I like the general breakdown of Power, Finesse, Resistance. I wish a more streamlined approach could have been managed with Werewolf so that the games would be more a like in structure. I enjoyed First Ed CWoD (with the exception of the handling of Vicissitude but that was rectifiable). I liked the underlying Meta which proposed all the conspiracies were true (even the ones that contradict), and backed by secret powers that hated and vied with each other for secret control of the results. I didn't care for the end of the world story, which given the vast universal power of the meta could have been more vastly universal - like a Michael Moorcock story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942358-trying-to-figure-out-what-this-means-to-me-cofd-vs-cwod?p=942362#post942362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The meta is just setting, you should have no problem putting it in your game in any system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't find this to be true. Systemic approaches to powers, to social divisions, etc. all infer and imply (both) a metathesis of action inherent to the philosophy not only of play, but also of theme and plot. When one obliterates the relationship of the Garou to the totemic spirits and sets their powers for the destruction and driving away of spirits, there is an inherent antipathy between the metas of the two systems. In system one, there is an inherent meta that the Universe is besouled and full of entities in a cosmic environmental cycle of interactions. It is the Rg Veda of Babylon cast upon the Millwheel of the Olmec calendar. The very description of the powers and social structures of NWoD are built to prevent this syncretic nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":2345,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","user":"Whithers","date":". 08-11-2016, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T14:56:34-07:00","id":948876,"title":"","content":"Well, your options are play CWoD, play NWoD/CofD, or try to bridge the gap between the two yourself. There's not really an alternative that gives you the setting and metaplot of CWoD with the streamlined mechanics of CofD. You could always wait for WoD 4th Edition and hope the rules changes streamline it in a way that suits your needs, but we have no real indication when that will be finished, or what it will look like when it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T15:03:40-07:00","id":948884,"title":"","content":"Translating between the two Worlds of Darkness is still feasible. However, nWoD/CofD is definitely its own setting, with rules flowing from that setting. It doesn't work as a generic urban fantasy system any more than cWoD does.<br /> <br /> The rules are fairly adaptable. If you want, for example, VtM stuff ported to VtR, the latter's forum is full of good conversions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 08-11-2016, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T00:27:41-07:00","id":953022,"title":"","content":"Appreciate the tips. Right now I am refereeing in TS in a different system while attempting to flesh out my own WoD city setting using multiple games. LOL, I may spend so much time imagining and writing about it that I never actually get to play.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T11:04:36-07:00","id":956432,"title":"","content":"It's doable but a pain in the butt. I would need to make some new systems to port Mage to the new system for instance to convert quiet and paradimgn","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1563-oriontyson","name":"OrionTyson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T13:19:22-07:00","id":958866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OrionTyson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942358-trying-to-figure-out-what-this-means-to-me-cofd-vs-cwod?p=956432#post956432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's doable but a pain in the butt. I would need to make some new systems to port Mage to the new system for instance to convert quiet and paradigm</div> </div> </div> </div>Quiet and Hubris are alternative approaches to the same event: Stop those pesky mages from reality ripping in front of the muggles. Either system could be used pretty much as is, given the similarities of stats, die usage, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}